<% content_for :title, "On Sciatica | Bipolar Sober" %>

<main class="toolbox-sciatica-page">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="toolbox-sciatica-hero">
    <div class="toolbox-sciatica-hero-content">

      <p class="toolbox-sciatica-eyebrow">
        BIPOLAR SOBER / TOOLBOX / ON SCIATICA
      </p>

      <h1>
        <span>WHEN YOUR</span>
        <span>BODY SAYS</span>
        <span>FUCK YOU.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="toolbox-sciatica-intro">
        PAIN. LIMITATIONS. FRUSTRATION.<br>
        AND TRYING TO HAVE A FUCKING LIFE ANYWAY.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- PAIN -->
  <section class="sciatica-section sciatica-section-pink">

    <div class="sciatica-section-number">
      01 / PAIN
    </div>

    <div class="sciatica-section-content">

      <h2>
        PAIN TAKES<br>
        UP FUCKING<br>
        SPACE.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Physical pain doesn't stay neatly inside one part of your body.
        It can change how you sleep, move, think, work, socialize,
        concentrate, and deal with everything else happening in your life.
      </p>

      <p>
        When pain keeps demanding your attention, ordinary things can
        suddenly require way more energy than they used to.
      </p>

      <div class="sciatica-callout">
        <p>
          YOU CAN ACKNOWLEDGE THAT THIS FUCKING SUCKS<br>
          WITHOUT MAKING IT YOUR ENTIRE IDENTITY.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- THE GRIEF -->
  <section class="sciatica-section sciatica-section-yellow">

    <div class="sciatica-section-number">
      02 / THE GRIEF
    </div>

    <div class="sciatica-section-content">

      <h2>
        I USED TO<br>
        JUST DO<br>
        THIS SHIT.
      </h2>

      <p>
        One of the strangest parts of physical limitations is remembering
        when you didn't have to think about them.
      </p>

      <p>
        Walking somewhere. Bending down. Standing around.
        Going out. Cleaning. Exercising. Sleeping.
      </p>

      <p>
        Things that used to be automatic can become calculations.
      </p>

      <div class="sciatica-big-question">
        CAN I DO IT?<br>
        HOW MUCH WILL IT HURT?<br>
        WHAT WILL IT COST ME LATER?
      </div>

      <p>
        Being angry or sad about that doesn't mean you've given up.
        Sometimes you're grieving something that genuinely changed.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- BAD DAYS -->
  <section class="sciatica-section sciatica-section-purple">

    <div class="sciatica-section-number">
      03 / BAD DAYS
    </div>

    <div class="sciatica-section-content">

      <h2>
        TODAY<br>
        FUCKING<br>
        HURTS.
      </h2>

      <p>
        A bad pain day has a nasty habit of turning itself into a prediction.
      </p>

      <div class="sciatica-before-after">

        <div>
          <p class="sciatica-label">THE THOUGHT</p>
          <p>IT'S THIS BAD TODAY. MY LIFE IS FUCKED.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p class="sciatica-label">THE RESET</p>
          <p>IT'S THIS BAD TODAY. TODAY IS WHAT I HAVE TO DEAL WITH.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p>
        You don't have to solve the rest of your life from the middle
        of today's worst moment.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- PACING -->
  <section class="sciatica-section sciatica-section-black">

    <div class="sciatica-section-number">
      04 / PACING
    </div>

    <div class="sciatica-section-content">

      <h2>
        DON'T SPEND<br>
        TOMORROW'S<br>
        FUCKING ENERGY.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Feeling a little better can make it tempting to do every single
        thing you've been unable to do.
      </p>

      <p>
        Then your body sends you the bill.
      </p>

      <div class="sciatica-tool-list">

        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <p>Decide what actually needs to happen today.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <p>Break bigger jobs into smaller pieces.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <p>Build breaks into the plan instead of waiting until you're wrecked.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <p>Notice what tends to make the rest of the day significantly harder.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>05</span>
          <p>Let "enough for today" actually be enough.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- PRODUCTIVITY -->
  <section class="sciatica-section sciatica-section-pink">

    <div class="sciatica-section-number">
      05 / PRODUCTIVITY
    </div>

    <div class="sciatica-section-content">

      <h2>
        YOU ARE NOT<br>
        A FUCKING<br>
        MACHINE.
      </h2>

      <p>
        When your body can't do what your brain planned, it's easy to
        interpret the difference as laziness or failure.
      </p>

      <p>
        But capacity changes.
      </p>

      <div class="sciatica-callout">
        <p>
          "I COULD HAVE DONE MORE"<br>
          IS NOT THE SAME AS<br>
          "DOING MORE WOULD HAVE BEEN GOOD FOR ME."
        </p>
      </div>

      <p>
        Some days are productive days.
        Some days are maintenance days.
        Some days the assignment is simply getting through the fucking day.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- ASKING FOR HELP -->
  <section class="sciatica-section sciatica-section-yellow">

    <div class="sciatica-section-number">
      06 / HELP
    </div>

    <div class="sciatica-section-content">

      <h2>
        LET SOMEBODY<br>
        CARRY THE<br>
        FUCKING BOX.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Independence can turn into stubbornness pretty quickly when
        asking for help feels like admitting defeat.
      </p>

      <p>
        Help doesn't have to mean surrendering your independence.
        Sometimes it means saving your limited energy for the shit
        only you can do.
      </p>

      <div class="sciatica-tool-list">

        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <p>Be specific about what would actually help.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <p>Stop apologizing five times for having a physical limitation.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <p>Use accommodations and tools that make life easier when they're available.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <p>Save your energy for things that matter more than proving you can suffer independently.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- PEOPLE -->
  <section class="sciatica-section sciatica-section-purple">

    <div class="sciatica-section-number">
      07 / OTHER PEOPLE
    </div>

    <div class="sciatica-section-content">

      <h2>
        "BUT YOU<br>
        LOOK<br>
        FINE."
      </h2>

      <p>
        Not every limitation is visible.
        And people who aren't inside your body don't automatically
        understand what something costs you physically.
      </p>

      <p>
        You don't have to perform pain convincingly enough to earn
        permission to take care of yourself.
      </p>

      <div class="sciatica-callout">
        <p>
          THEY DON'T HAVE TO FEEL IT<br>
          FOR YOU TO FUCKING FEEL IT.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- PAIN + MOOD -->
  <section class="sciatica-section sciatica-section-black">

    <div class="sciatica-section-number">
      08 / PAIN + YOUR HEAD
    </div>

    <div class="sciatica-section-content">

      <h2>
        YOUR BODY<br>
        AND BRAIN<br>
        FUCKING TALK.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Persistent pain can affect mood, stress, patience, sleep,
        concentration, and how much emotional bandwidth you have left.
      </p>

      <p>
        And when you're already dealing with mental health or recovery,
        physical pain can become another thing your coping system
        has to carry.
      </p>

      <div class="sciatica-tool-list">

        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <p>Notice when pain is changing your mood.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <p>Notice when poor sleep is making everything feel worse.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <p>Notice when frustration starts becoming hopelessness.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <p>Notice when pain starts making old escape behaviors look attractive again.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p>
        The earlier you notice the connection, the earlier you can use
        whatever support belongs in your actual treatment and recovery plan.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- RECOVERY -->
  <section class="sciatica-section sciatica-section-pink">

    <div class="sciatica-section-number">
      09 / PAIN + RECOVERY
    </div>

    <div class="sciatica-section-content">

      <h2>
        I WANT<br>
        FUCKING<br>
        RELIEF.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Physical pain can make the desire for immediate relief incredibly loud.
      </p>

      <p>
        If pain has been connected to drinking, using, or other escape
        behaviors before, don't wait until you're desperate to decide
        how you're going to cope with a bad pain day.
      </p>

      <div class="sciatica-big-question">
        WHAT DO I NEED<br>
        FROM THIS MOMENT —<br>
        RELIEF, REST, HELP,<br>
        DISTRACTION, OR ESCAPE?
      </div>

      <p>
        Those aren't always the same thing.
      </p>

      <div class="sciatica-callout">
        <p>
          PAIN MAY BE THE TRIGGER.<br>
          THE NEXT MOVE IS STILL A CHOICE.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- CONTROL -->
  <section class="sciatica-section sciatica-section-yellow">

    <div class="sciatica-section-number">
      10 / CONTROL
    </div>

    <div class="sciatica-section-content">

      <h2>
        WHAT CAN<br>
        I DO<br>
        TODAY?
      </h2>

      <div class="sciatica-control-grid">

        <div>
          <p class="sciatica-label">MAYBE MINE</p>

          <p>How I structure today.</p>
          <p>Whether I ask for help.</p>
          <p>Whether I use my coping tools.</p>
          <p>Whether I communicate my limits.</p>
          <p>Whether I follow my treatment plan.</p>
          <p>How I talk to myself about this.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p class="sciatica-label">NOT MINE</p>

          <p>Having pain today.</p>
          <p>Other people's opinions about it.</p>
          <p>How quickly my body improves.</p>
          <p>Everything I wish I could do.</p>
          <p>The fact that this is frustrating.</p>
          <p>Knowing exactly what the future looks like.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- MEDICAL CARE -->
  <section class="sciatica-section sciatica-section-purple">

    <div class="sciatica-section-number">
      11 / GETTING CARE
    </div>

    <div class="sciatica-section-content">

      <h2>
        COPING ISN'T<br>
        THE SAME AS<br>
        IGNORING IT.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Coping tools can help you live through pain.
        They aren't a substitute for getting medical symptoms evaluated
        or following an appropriate treatment plan.
      </p>

      <p>
        Keep track of meaningful changes in symptoms and bring them to
        the professionals treating you instead of assuming you just have
        to tough everything out.
      </p>

      <div class="sciatica-callout">
        <p>
          "I CAN COPE WITH THIS"<br>
          DOESN'T MEAN<br>
          "I SHOULDN'T GET CARE FOR THIS."
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- BAD DAY PLAN -->
  <section class="sciatica-section sciatica-section-black">

    <div class="sciatica-section-number">
      12 / BAD DAY PLAN
    </div>

    <div class="sciatica-section-content">

      <h2>
        TODAY<br>
        FUCKING<br>
        SUCKS. NOW WHAT?
      </h2>

      <div class="sciatica-workbook">

        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>CHECK IN</h3>
          <p>What is my body telling me today?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>PRIORITIZE</h3>
          <p>What actually needs to happen?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>ADJUST</h3>
          <p>What can be changed, shortened, postponed, or delegated?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <h3>NOTICE</h3>
          <p>What is the pain doing to my mood and thinking?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>05</span>
          <h3>SUPPORT</h3>
          <p>Who or what do I need today?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>06</span>
          <h3>STOP</h3>
          <p>What would tell me I've done enough for today?</p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- ENDING -->
  <section class="sciatica-ending">

    <p class="sciatica-ending-small">
      YOUR BODY CAN LIMIT WHAT YOU DO WITHOUT DEFINING WHO YOU ARE.
    </p>

    <h2>
      THIS HURTS.<br>
      THIS SUCKS.<br>
      I'M STILL HERE.
    </h2>

    <p>
      Adjust the plan. Ask for help. Be pissed off when you're pissed off.
      Take care of the body you're actually living in — not the one you
      think you should have today.
    </p>

    <%= link_to "← BACK TO TOOLBOX",
        toolbox_path,
        class: "sciatica-back-link" %>

  </section>

</main>